ard for most modern combat snipers in US/NATO that are targeting humans in the open and not nearly that far away).<br /> <br /> There only fourteen people in history known to have killed someone at a mile or farther with a rifle (and again, they all had at least a spotter with them if not more help). This also skips ahead to one of the best defenses against this: it almost never happens. In centuries of using explosions to hurl metal at people, this is basically a fluke occurrence where dozens of factors have to line up perfectly for the shooter to even consider pulling the trigger at those sorts of ranges. Supernatural powers can also only do so much about many of the reasons why this is so rare:<br /> <br /> 1) These guns are huge. The Accuracy International rifle used in NATO armed forces chambered for the .338 weighs 15 lbs unloaded and without optics, and is 40 inches long. The Barret .50 (the most famous .50 sniper rifle as much as one can call it a sniper rifle) is 33 lbs unloaded and no optics and 57 inches long. These are not guns you walk around with and then bring up to your shoulder and shoot when you see a target. These are not guns you tuck under a trench coat. The whole &quot;assemble on site out of a briefcase&quot; thing in movies doesn't work, because that can completely throw off your aim at long ranges because the barrel is aligned 1mm off from where it was before. Obviously supernaturals have powers that can help with a lot of these issues, but it's still a lot of work just to get these rifles into position.<br /> <br /> 2) Once you're talking about extreme range shooting lots of things start coming into play. One of the reasons huge bullets are used (even the .338 is a beast), is for the inertia the bullet has, not because of the giant holes giant bullets make. Over these sorts of distance the bullet can travel through multiple microclimates. wind might be blowing 5 mph to the east for a bit, and then 10 mph to the west for another, and the bullet with sway in its path over that long of a shot. The bullet passing over different surfaces means going through air of different temperatures which causes vertical deflections. Shit like the Coriolis effect can even matter at the longer ranges of rifle shooting.<br /> <br /> 3) Most targets are moving. If it takes you 2 minutes to get yourself in place, and 30 seconds to do all the math on your shot... you might have completely missed the chance. Even if you were setup ahead of time, doing all of the calculations (again, these people work in teams for a reason) while a target is moving is nearly impossible (and Celerity or Rage isn't going to help you there).</div> </div> </div> </div>1000 Meter Club, thank you. My brain kept going to &quot;One Mile Club&quot; but I wasn't sure enough to even suggest it when I posted.<br /> <br /> I spent a little bit of time learning about sniping as a geek/gamer thing when I was younger, so I used to know some of this, but it definitely wasn't in my mind when I posed the question. Between the extreme skill level required and limited uses, I can definitely see where it remains more of a special niche rather than general dominant-strategy. The one-mile shot isn't necessarily the most important case, it just happened to be the one that came to mind between the scene in BJD and the other thread that got me thinking about this included mention of an anti-materiel rifle specifically. As you noted with the prevalence of the .338, even focusing on the .50 cal. is probably mostly coming from a &quot;overkill = good&quot; attitude towards dealing with supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a difficulty 8 roll, and each success only heals one level of damage. If our vampire sniper is familiar with WtA werewolves (or you're a WtA sniper), and is skilled enough to one-shot at thos ranges? You just double tap (Celerity or Rage are very useful for that part): the first shot triggers the roll to stay active, they Frenzy (so no taking cover from your second shot) but only have a few HLs back, and then you shoot a second time and they don't get to roll again that scene. The harder part is consistently doing that kind of damage against a werewolf since very few splats have ways to seriously increase the damage of firearms (and Werewolves soak Agg with their full Stamina in a combat form, so you need a lot of damage dice... or a bit fewer and silver bullets).<br /> <br /> Of course, for the sake of a vampire story, the Garou could have just failed the Rage roll and died. With Diff 8, it's going to happen to most werewolves eventually if they try to rely on that backup regen too much. So it's not some ludicrous WtA ignoring thing for that roll to not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the Difficulty and the fact that you only get one roll for it per turn, yeah, I can see that it's not something you can lean on too heavily. It complicates ambushes if you're really counting on them staying down after the first shot, but it's not insurmountable by any stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends where you live? They're completely legal in 46 US states, and only banned in California and Washington DC. Beyond things like background checks and so on, the big difficulty is that they're expensive. A true military grade .50 cal sniper rifle with all the fixings is easily going to cost ~$20K... and the bullets aren't cheap either. If you needed to be budget sensitive, you can get a .50 cal hunting rifle for closer to $5K (though not all of those can handle the higher end sniper .50 cal rounds). For getting one good shot off, the big thing you're lacking is high end optics (but that's one of the easiest things for supernaturals to get around), but you're going to be in trouble when people notice you and your giant gun, since you'll be very constrained in defending yourself (though most military snipers just carry an assault rifle and switch to that if it turns into that sort of situation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was probably being more hand-wavey than I should have been; I was kind of including the cost in the general notion of availability.<br /> <br /> When I first read what you said about military-grade sniper rifles being legal in most places, my impulse was to make a pithy comment about how different things can be between the USA and Canada (where I live). But I decided to do a double-check, since this isn't actually something I've really looked into before, and it turns out that it may actually be legal here as well? Getting mixed signals from a brief bit of Googling, though it looks like it may be the sort of thing that changed given the newer gun control laws that have come in recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem goes back to how much supernatural powers can make up for the difficulty of using these sorts of weapons practically. You're already looking at training two people on an incredibly expensive piece of hardware that costs a decent chunk of change for every practice shot ($3 to $5 per bullet should be expected). Training a supernatural that can mean reducing the need for a spotter is a huge saving in time, energy, and financial costs. Supernaturals are also going to be able to escape with their huge expensive rifles far more easily. Relying on mortals/minion splats is a big risk for something so intensive anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm not necessarily suggesting that this should primarily be viewed as a method of balancing things between supernaturals and non-supernaturals/minion-splats. The people who already possess the necessary skills would potentially be valuable allies/servants, but training them up from scratch probably makes more sense only in specific contexts, based on everything you've pointed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have the advantage of being magically less impacted by guns (though the ST might rule otherwise for these sorts of firearms), and there aren't that many ways to make bullets do agg (though with something like WtA Talens that's a bit ST dependent, but the examples in the books don't really support just a flat out upgrade like that; mages and changelings are more troublesome as snipers... but they need sniping for these things even less anyway). Vampires are also naturally night time city dwellers. SWAT snipers don't bother training in shooting beyond 300m because cities and suburbs never provide that kind of clear line of sight. Most militarized police around the world aren't allowed to shoot farther than 100m without explicit permission because populated areas have too many complications for the risk. Most powerful vampires don't have to worry about being sniped from a mile away because cities are natural cover, and the closer the sniper has to be, the more those big honking .50 cals aren't practical even with some supernatural boosts.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are difficult because beyond their innate powers (which do have some decent defenses against this) their bought powers are all over the place. One werewolf might have zero supernatural defenses against guns, while another might have a bunch of things to make sure they don't get shot (there's a sample Talen in one of the books that's an example of Talens made for kinfolk to be able to use without Gnosis, that reflexively acts as cover if someone tries to shoot them, so that sort of trick is certainly available to the shifters). The Garou also gather in more rural areas, where long range shooting is more viable, but the Garou have access to lots of supernatural senses that means being a mile or two away is zero guarantee one doesn't notice you. So it's a big mixed bag. IME though, because the Garou are sensitive to things like humans shooting at wolves, they tend to think about guns in their territories more than other splats. But that doesn't mean they're prepared for full splat supernatural offensive snipers (defensive ones are a different matter since Pentex as those).<br /> <br /> Mages come down to the normal issue of mages: if they're prepared, you might as well not bother. If you actually surprise them, they can crumple fast. Their versatility does mean it's not hard for them to have one or two spells going to defend themselves against attacks. Mages can also be very tricky because most other supernaturals aren't great at spotting true magic. A mage in a business suit might have an armor rating of 8 without it being an active effect that would ping most other splats reflexive senses, or even get picked up as specifically super-armored clothing by active senses. As well, with the Technocracy around, guns are very much on the minds of mages as a threat to be wary of. Mages make for ridiculously good snipers if they're willing to use guns, so mages that don't want to get sniped by a Technocrat (including other Technocrats worried about internal strife) are going to want something in case they're in a sniper's crosshairs.<br /> <br /> Changelings would be great snipers if most of them didn't suck with making magical modern weapons. They also have a lot of good ways to defend themselves against snipers... but very little reason to bother unless prompted. While they like to be around people, offering many of the advantages vampires have for it being difficult to position a high powered rifle in the first place, it's just less on their radar because it's not really a threat they regularly face. They're not built like the tougher splats, so hiring a bunch of thugs with pistols is generally more effective so you can overwhelm their defenses with numbers instead of the one shot one kill with massive damage that they might be able to deflect on the fly.<br /> <br /> Wraiths... not really part of the equation rally.<br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei are pretty much in the same position as western vampires.<br /> <br /> The Imbued are generally just screwed against this kind of attack. Though if one of them has Bluster it can completely stymie a sniper for long enough for the group to get out of harm's way. Though, like changelings, they're not sturdy enough to really worry about all this time and effort for a massive sniper rifle. A small gang of normal humans with smaller guns are far more dangerous (and Bluster can't stop lots of attacks at once) because you don't need to worry about all of the effort of getting an elite sniper.<br /> <br /> Demons are a weird case because they have insane sensory powers for supernatural shenanigans, but they are (or at least can be) tough enough to justify wanting high end firepower. They're probably the one time where a highly trained mortal assassin with big gun is actually the way to go. But like the Garou their powers are all over the place and it can be really hard speculate on because some are going to be screwed in these situations, and some can basically flip your shooter off and walk away.<br /> <br /> Living Orpheus agents are pretty screwed... but you just turned them into a ghost that has a strong reason to want you dead and isn't bound by the laws of the Underworld like a normal wraith. If you can't make anti-ghost bullets... this will probably backfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that you brought up the more common ranges used in urban sniping, by SWAT for example. To the extent that I ponder whether or not sniping serves as a way of &quot;leveling the playing field,&quot; it actually is more in terms of how widely available the tactic is, theoretically. As you've demonstrated, the kind of skill level required for the mile-long shot is outside the reach of all but the most dedicated specialists (and their support teams), but the level of marksmanship needed to hit something at less than half that range with a good scope would probably be fairly less. But you'd therefore have less space between you and any allies of the target if you're not trying to assassinate a lone individual, which significantly increases the risk of not being able to escape. The more viable the tactic becomes for mass-adoption, the less differentiated it becomes from any other bunch of people with guns.<br /> <br /> Most of what you had to say about vampires was pretty straightforward, but the point about shooting at night was good; hadn't considered that it seriously complicates matters for any sniper that doesn't have a (probably supernatural) solution for that, especially with the challenges at extreme ranges.<br /> <br /> The point about Garou senses is a really great one; I hadn't considered the extent to which they could negate the element of surprise. A sniper specifically targeting werewolves would need to account for that somehow if they wanted to get the drop on one. Definitely understand the ways in which the variety of Gifts, Fetishes, etc., available to the Garou makes the viability of just about any strategy dependent on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> I almost opted to simply exclude Mages from the discussion, just because the countermeasures available to them are nearly endless. But I'm kind of glad that I didn't, because the discussion of Awakened snipers made think about the fun fact that a Mage sniper could either use their magic to enhance their mundane shooting with a sniper rifle, OR they could just use it as an Instrument for an Effect instead, which is kind of neat.<br /> <br /> I don't really know much about Changelings beyond the very basic stuff, so I didn't have much knowledge to work with on that front, and your input was especially helpful!<br /> <br /> I must admit I really hadn't given much thought to the other splats, though I do know them a little better. Except Orpheus, never spent much time on that. Not surprised that the Imbued are just kind of hooped; their whole thing is being normal people with just a bit of anti-supernatural Kryptonite up their sleeve. Nor am I surprised that the Fallen, like the Garou, are hard to peg down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think they make the playing field even worse. The splats that have the best sniper tools are also the splats that have the best sniper countermeasures. A well built gun-bunny Garou can wreck vampires like their klaive wielding brethren even if it might be a bit more convoluted and/or limited to get there...and for once the Umbra is a great benefit because getting into the Umbra after shooting a major enemy when you're very far away is actually practical much earlier than &quot;hop out of the Umbra, claw claw claw, hop back into the Umbra&quot; will be. Glass Walkers (because if you're going guns and Garou, you want a Glass Walker or a Silver Fang with Glass Walker friends but Silver Fang gun users aren't terribly popular in their Tribe despite them getting firearm boosting stuff in their Gift list) have a lot of easy access to anti-gun countermeasures as well.<br /> <br /> This even goes internally as well. As I noted Technocrats have great guns, great firearms training, and great access to anti-magical-bullet materials as well. I've also had to remind an Akashic player before that mastering unarmed combat in the modern world does not mean people aren't going to shoot guns... and that went unheeded to very bad results. &quot;I know Do&quot; doesn't make you Neo... but the Euthanatos have no problem training to be Deadshot (sure Suicide Squad sucked, but that ricochet shot at the beginning of the movie is literally a rote in the Revied Euthie book) and going gun-fu on anyone silly enough to forget what era this is.<br /> <br /> So the sniper-alpha strike isn't really a great check on supernaturals because it tends to just exacerbate the strengths of supernatural alpha-strikes once they get mixed together.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the extent that I thought sniper rifles might balance things out, it wasn't because I thought that the average sniper could be equal to the power of a dedicated supernatural alpha strike, sniper or otherwise, but rather the idea that the skill level required for less extreme examples of sniping might be more achievable for the members of various splats than the combination of supernatural abilities you would need to perform a similar attack with a comparable amount of risk. But, aside from the realization above about the increasing risks that come from accepting reductions in range, I also realize that attempting this tactic with less skill decreases the likelihood that you'll finish the target in the first shot, which is the whole point of an alpha strike.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding the Akashic and putting all their eggs in the Do-basket: how *dare* you make such a reasonable point! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I myself am a bit guilty of being overly fond of martial arts over weapon skills in RPGs and such, so I could definitely see myself falling into that trap.<br /> <br /> Once again, thank you for taking the time to go over all of that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T02:08:57-08:00","id":1527109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527099#post1527099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...coming from a &quot;overkill = good&quot; attitude towards dealing with supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That by itself isn't always the worse thing to keep in mind, but I as went it, what your fighting impacts this a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between the Difficulty and the fact that you only get one roll for it per turn, yeah, I can see that it's not something you can lean on too heavily. It complicates ambushes if you're really counting on them staying down after the first shot, but it's not insurmountable by any stretch. </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify: it's once per scene, not once a turn. So it's very limited.<br /> <br /> In fact, it's not hard to flip around into a positive for the shooter, because the Garou automatically Frenzies (and that means they have to take on the Crinos or Hispo form). Garou in a Frenzy will attack the nearest available target (depending on their stats that might not include their pack, and there are some tricks to extend it to more characters, but that's still pretty limited). One of my Garou that was a scout/sniper purposefully targeted high Rage enemies so they're heal up and Frenzy because it sows chaos (and being a sniper he was never the nearest target even if the shot revealed he existed). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I first read what you said about military-grade sniper rifles being legal in most places, my impulse was to make a pithy comment about how different things can be between the USA and Canada (where I live). But I decided to do a double-check, since this isn't actually something I've really looked into before, and it turns out that it may actually be legal here as well? Getting mixed signals from a brief bit of Googling, though it looks like it may be the sort of thing that changed given the newer gun control laws that have come in recently. </div> </div> </div>One of the complexities of writing gun laws is that &quot;sniper rifle&quot; isn't really a well defined class of weapon. Now, especially in countries that aren't the US, it's very easy to regulate surplus military gear from resale to the general public (here in the US, the military can sell old guns to civilians.. because we're exceptional or something). So in Canada (sorry, I don't know the specifics as well there myself) it might be illegal to buy the military version of a rifle, but legal to buy a civilian model that has a few features stripped off. I know .50 cal hunting rifles (and remember that sniper rifles started as hunting rifles that slowly evolved for military use) aren't hard to get in Canada because you need guns that powerful in rural areas to deal with bears or moose that are being a threat to human livelihood (even if getting professionals to relocate animals is preferred, the more rural the harder that is to count on in a timely fashion). Most countries also just have less strict laws around long arms than handguns, because of the whole &quot;big guns are obvious&quot; part of the equation. Most gun related deaths (even in countries with lots of good laws on this) are still handguns... so that's where the primary legal focus tends to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The more viable the tactic becomes for mass-adoption, the less differentiated it becomes from any other bunch of people with guns. </div> </div> </div>Well, to diverge a bit from sniping, IMO, if you combine both real world tactics and the peculiarities of the WoD combat systems, there is one &quot;mundane&quot; alpha strike option that stands out: a well trained fire team (that is generally four soldiers, with a small level of specialization between them). There's a reason why this is the dominant paradigm of modern combat. Firearms tech (esp. compared to defensive tech) is so good, that small squads that know what they're doing are one of the best ways to ensure you do as much damage as possible to a target. There are trade-offs of course, but they have far more versatility than a dedicated sniper unit, so they can adapt more rapidly to a situation. They can use carbines or SMGs in denser areas for stealth/ease of mobility, or use plenty powerful assault rifles and so on for situations where there's less risk involved with being a bunch of people with guns obviously ready to shoot something. A fireteam usually has a dedicated marksman that acts as a &quot;light&quot; sniper, and the rest of the team can help as spotters and look outs if you only really need one clean shot. Or they can open up with an overwhelming amount of firepower (esp. in one squad member brings a SAW) as a group to attack multiple targets, or vastly increase the odds that one target gets hit with enough bullets they're done for.<br /> <br /> In the WoD, the mechanics favor this a lot as it is, and it gives different splats more options. A squad can be composed of relatively amateur disposable assets and still d a lot of damage, or it can be a dedicate group of full supernaturals that turn into John Wick x 4 when the shooting starts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of what you had to say about vampires was pretty straightforward, but the point about shooting at night was good; hadn't considered that it seriously complicates matters for any sniper that doesn't have a (probably supernatural) solution for that, especially with the challenges at extreme ranges. </div> </div> </div>We have very good nighttime optics these days (even in the civilian market). What night really messes with is finding environmental cues. In open terrain during the day, there are lots of things to help visual conditions all along the path of the bullet. Flags or tall plants blowing in the wind, visible heat distortions, etc. Cities and night time, even with the best night vision, just means it's a lot harder to find those sorts of details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again, thank you for taking the time to go over all of that! </div> </div> </div>Glad to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T22:18:28-08:00","id":1530136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have the advantage of being magically less impacted by guns (though the ST might rule otherwise for these sorts of firearms), and there aren't that many ways to make bullets do agg (though with something like WtA Talens that's a bit ST dependent, but the examples in the books don't really support just a flat out upgrade like that; mages and changelings are more troublesome as snipers... but they need sniping for these things even less anyway). Vampires are also naturally night time city dwellers. SWAT snipers don't bother training in shooting beyond 300m because cities and suburbs never provide that kind of clear line of sight. Most militarized police around the world aren't allowed to shoot farther than 100m without explicit permission because populated areas have too many complications for the risk. Most powerful vampires don't have to worry about being sniped from a mile away because cities are natural cover, and the closer the sniper has to be, the more those big honking .50 cals aren't practical even with some supernatural boosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have also the advantage that (at least in V20) their most common defence (Fortitude) is always active and by spending one point of Blood they can turn give them self automatic successess to the Soak role equal equal to to their Fortitude rating. So unless the sniper can fir multiple time before the vampire can find cover, there is good chance that a somewhat experienced vampire would survive.<br /> <br /> I think there is also at least one power (not sure if it was a combination discipline or and elder discipline) that would allow a vampire to reflexively turn into mist when attacked, but that's of course pretty rare.<br /> <br /> A high end Vampire sniper is also pretty scarry in V20, Celerity boosts your dexterity and there is a elder discipline that adds your celerity as outomatic successess to the damage role of a firearm.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to aggrevated damage I think it depends a bit on the ST, there are some types of mundane ammunition (ike incendiary rounds) of .50cal where one could argue tat they do aggrevated against Vampires, but but afaik there are no rules about that.<br /> <br /> And in case of Werewolf these is of course the question if you can get Silver Bullet for a Sniper Rifle.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 02-07-2024, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T00:08:42-08:00","id":1530140,"title":"","content":"Incendiary rounds dealing agg to vampires really depends on how cinematic the ST wants to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Realistically&quot; the concept is silly. High power incendiary rounds wouldn't be in contact with a human-ish target for long enough to actually cause burns from the chemicals (keeping in mind that bullet wounds do release considerable heat as it is just from the physicals of metal hitting wet flesh). Incendiary rounds were invented for and are still exclusively designed for, &quot;hard&quot; targets such as vehicles and supply caches. Only the oldest incendiary rounds don't rely on hitting something hard enough to stop high powered rounds (the deformation on impact is what then brings the incendiary charge in contact with the compromised armor) because they were shooting at hydrogen dirigibles and... you don't need a lot of fire to cause massive damage to those.<br /> <br /> Even the very Internet famous dragon's breath shotgun rounds are really not going to do much to a vampire (though Rotshreck risks should be real) because the heat isn't continuous it's a short burst of very high heat with minimal ability to penetrate the human body (esp. bony parts like the chest or skull), and no way to keep the heat on the target long enough to cause it to catch fire. to try to put it in some perspective, if you shot a person in the stomach (no pesky bones) at point blank range to maximize the damage, you're create a half-orange sized section of extremely burnt flesh, while doing basically nothing physically to the rest of the body. Now, that's certainly an extremely serious wound to a human (depending on how much fat they have in their belly, they could have some intestinal damage, as high grade burns are slow to heal and major sources of secondary infections), but you're not going to kill them on the spot, or send them up in a gout of flame. It's far less deadly than a normal 12 gauge buckshot or deer slug, as it might not even be incapacitating in the heat of a fight.<br /> <br /> So realistically anything short of an actual flamethrower should really be dealing a few levels of fire damage at worst. We have things like flamethrowers precisely because small metal bits flying at high speeds are hard to jam any serious amount of incendiary material in, let alone make effective against a human-ish target.<br /> <br /> If one wants to be a bit more cinematic about it, of course it's easy enough to say that fire is a bane of vampires and they're more impacted that physics says they should be because it's a metaphysical curse.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> On silver bullets, besides how expensive silver is, the simple solution is to cast and load your own silver ammunition. Silver isn't actually a bad metal for bullets on its own, but it requires a completely different set of casting tools than convention bullet metals use. Once you have the appropriate casting setup (and the money for all that silver), loading a casing with gunpowder isn't any different. There's a lot of Internet debates on things like how much wear and tear silver bullets would do to the barrel and rifling, but not a lot of people have the money to pop off a few hundred silver bullets to determine what a proper maintenance regimen should be for silver ammunition in a modern barrel (or if there might be better alternative barrel designs).<br /> <br /> Though, that all said, the discussion was a bit more the other way of werewolves using their powers to create guns/bullets that do aggravated damage to other supernaturals that aren't weak to silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:12:03-08:00","id":1530169,"title":"","content":"Dragon'sbreaths might not be able to transfer through the skull, but most skulls have some huge gaps inconveniently made in their front-facing structure. Taking out a vampire's eyes should be possible (as well as other character types' eyes, but Garou can potentially turn that damage into bashing with a Gift and are generally quite resilient, and if you use it against a Solimond you're just going to caress them).<br /> <br /> Regarding incendiary rounds meant for use against hard targets, would that potentially increase their performance against high-Fortitude vampires? Or is it all magic and I should really just relax?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T11:27:06-08:00","id":1530185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530140#post1530140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incendiary rounds dealing agg to vampires really depends on how cinematic the ST wants to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Realistically&quot; the concept is silly. High power incendiary rounds wouldn't be in contact with a human-ish target for long enough to actually cause burns from the chemicals (keeping in mind that bullet wounds do release considerable heat as it is just from the physicals of metal hitting wet flesh). Incendiary rounds were invented for and are still exclusively designed for, &quot;hard&quot; targets such as vehicles and supply caches. Only the oldest incendiary rounds don't rely on hitting something hard enough to stop high powered rounds (the deformation on impact is what then brings the incendiary charge in contact with the compromised armor) because they were shooting at hydrogen dirigibles and... you don't need a lot of fire to cause massive damage to those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know it is not particularly realistic, but the effects of weapons in RPGs are often not particualrly realistic.<br /> <br /> And it might be possible to come up with some sort of incideary or explosive projectile that works on a &quot;soft target&quot;.<br /> <br /> And at least Elder Vampires have some powers that might turn them into hard targets.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T11:44:58-08:00","id":1530187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530140#post1530140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On silver bullets, besides how expensive silver is, the simple solution is to cast and load your own silver ammunition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver isn't that expensive, current price about 720$ per kilo, which would be enough for about 20 .50 can bullets (and much more in smaller calibers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530140#post1530140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver isn't actually a bad metal for bullets on its own, but it requires a completely different set of casting tools than convention bullet metals use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit sceptical if you can simple cast ammunition for a sniper rifle, if you really want to hit a person at a distance of 1km and above, you will likely need a more precise method of manufacturing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530140#post1530140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, that all said, the discussion was a bit more the other way of werewolves using their powers to create guns/bullets that do aggravated damage to other supernaturals that aren't weak to silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think one should keep in mind that it is way more simple to make bullets that deal aggravated damage to Werewolfs that it is for other super naturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T12:01:18-08:00","id":1530188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530187#post1530187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver isn't that expensive, current price about 720$ per kilo, which would be enough for about 20 .50 can bullets (and much more in smaller calibers).<br /> <br /> I'm a bit sceptical if you can simple cast ammunition for a sniper rifle, if you really want to hit a person at a distance of 1km and above, you will likely need a more precise method of manufacturing.<br /> <br /> But I think one should keep in mind that it is way more simple to make bullets that deal aggravated damage to Werewolfs that it is for other super naturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the distance that sniper rifles are intended to fire from, Garou might actually get quite a generous warning time. At 1 klick and up, just under three seconds elapse between the pull of the trigger and the round reaching the target. Against someone with supernatural senses, that's conceivable enough time to let them dodge. At further distances, the speed of sound is going to continue to be your enemy.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Garou can make fetish guns at about the same level of potency as a klaive that work like ranged fang daggers, only having a higher base damage, usually. There's also a much less complicated talen called The Slug that does about the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T12:48:58-08:00","id":1530196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530169#post1530169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon'sbreaths might not be able to transfer through the skull, but most skulls have some huge gaps inconveniently made in their front-facing structure. Taking out a vampire's eyes should be possible (as well as other character types' eyes, but Garou can potentially turn that damage into bashing with a Gift and are generally quite resilient, and if you use it against a Solimond you're just going to caress them).<br /> <br /> Regarding incendiary rounds meant for use against hard targets, would that potentially increase their performance against high-Fortitude vampires? Or is it all magic and I should really just relax?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, starting at the end:<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're probably better relaxing and just calling it all magic.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the books are very vague on what Fortitude actually &quot;does.&quot; Part of this is that damage in the game is also very abstract; or more important the game focuses on the &quot;kind&quot; of wound inflicted rather than how the wound was inflict where the &quot;how&quot; is much more important to real world countermeasures.<br /> <br /> If Fortitude literally makes your tissues denser and thus more resilient to damage, realistically high Fortitude would actually make modern HEAP rounds more effective (though HEAP rounds don't come in standard infantry rifle sizes, and can't really be sized down below much). If Fortitude just makes a physical damage mean less to a vampire as their blood can force their undead bodies to operate despite missing bits that would be vital to human motion, then high powered rounds would continue to pass right through them (though Aahz does bring up a power that does explicitly harden vampires so that's a consideration).<br /> <br /> So the realism depends on interpreting a very ambiguous part of the game... so best to call it magic and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530185#post1530185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it might be possible to come up with some sort of incideary or explosive projectile that works on a &quot;soft target&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are. But there are limitations while still staying in the realm of a &quot;gun&quot; or anything that's going to be accurate at range. I would imagine hunters that are limited to relatively realistic technology that wanted to burn a vampire from a distance would be more focused on things like drones as the only real limitations on a drone carrying a payload of incendiary materials (which would also destroy most evidence of where the drone came from) is the weight the drone can handle. Drones are ubiquitous enough, and cities are loud enough, that it would be far easier as a tactic than R&amp;D on giving infantry/etc. &quot;fire&quot; bullets of some sort.<br /> <br /> To give an idea of the best someone has really come up with so far, there's a shotgun shell that deploys a fin-stabilized slug that's actually a glorified paintball casing filled with a binary incendiary (that is, when the paintball casing hits a &quot;soft&quot; target it breaks, and mixes two inert chemicals that then combine into an incendiary reaction). The power of the shotgun shell and the fins give it some range... but last I looked they weren't accurate beyond ~50m in ideal conditions.<br /> <br /> The essential problem for people that are stuck with technology, is that bullets are already small. Fitting an explosive/incendiary in them of any meaningful power means drastically increasing the size of the bullet, which either massively decreases accuracy, or increases the size of the weapon. If the weapon gets bigger than a shoulder mounted missile launcher... you can probably just use the missile; you're far into weapons people only see on the battlefield well beyond things like US's gun issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530187#post1530187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver isn't that expensive, current price about 720$ per kilo, which would be enough for about 20 .50 can bullets (and much more in smaller calibers).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not cheap? For snipers, they need to practice thousands of times with any changes to their setup (as long distances means you need to understand the differences in how different bullet materials will react to microclimate conditions). You can't just swag high end composite matchgrade ammo for silver ammo on a sniper and expect one-shot perfect accuracy at extreme ranges because you're messing with variables.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm a bit sceptical if you can simple cast ammunition for a sniper rifle, if you really want to hit a person at a distance of 1km and above, you will likely need a more precise method of manufacturing. </div> </div> </div>Casting is a highly refined practice in single-metal bullet manufacturing. Silver is the problem, not casting as a practice. Lead is cast very easily to high tolerances. Silver is difficult because it cools very rapidly, and silver can get &quot;sticky&quot; with many traditional mold materials. Using lead casting tools would get you garbage silver castings. Having a casting block that can maintain a proper temperature during pouring to make sure the silver doesn't cool until the mold is full, and lining it with graphite powder so the silver doesn't bind to the mold the general problems.<br /> <br /> The conical bullet is not a terribly difficult shape. People have been custom casting them for decades. Some professional shooters like to control even this level of their craft.<br /> <br /> What gets complicated is moving into things like jacketed rounds and composite materials, but those are irrelevant to a silver bullet that needs to be mostly pure metallic silver as WtA demands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I think one should keep in mind that it is way more simple to make bullets that deal aggravated damage to Werewolfs that it is for other super naturals. </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> The discussion is the effectiveness of &quot;alpha strikes&quot; against supernatural targets using mundane means. Silver is part of the consideration for werewolves of course, but high powered rifles can easily do enough lethal damage to kill a werewolf: 8 soak dice doesn't mean that much against 12 damage dealt when you've only got 7 HLs. Silver makes it easier for other types of strikes (because you can use tactics that don't require massive guns that do massive damage), but silver also has drawbacks that aren't inherently mitigated by bypassing some soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T23:21:14-08:00","id":1530786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530188#post1530188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the distance that sniper rifles are intended to fire from, Garou might actually get quite a generous warning time. At 1 klick and up, just under three seconds elapse between the pull of the trigger and the round reaching the target. Against someone with supernatural senses, that's conceivable enough time to let them dodge. At further distances, the speed of sound is going to continue to be your enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really since unless you use super sonic amuntion, bullets are faster than the sound. The speed of sound is roughly 300m/s .50BMG has a muzzel velocity in the region of 900m/s.<br /> The the muzzel flash might give you away of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530188#post1530188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, Garou can make fetish guns at about the same level of potency as a klaive that work like ranged fang daggers,</div> </div> </div> </div>Is something like that actually in the rules?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T23:40:26-08:00","id":1530787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530786#post1530786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really since unless you use super sonic amuntion, bullets are faster than the sound. The speed of sound is roughly 300m/s .50BMG has a muzzel velocity in the region of 900m/s.<br /> The the muzzel flash might give you away of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming you meant subsonic there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is something like that actually in the rules?<br /> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Check the entry for The Slug in the talens of Hammer and Klaive. It's a footnote to it, oddly enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T01:06:21-08:00","id":1530791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530787#post1530787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming you meant subsonic there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah of course.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T13:15:54-08:00","id":1530842,"title":"","content":"If you want to get a deep look at the differences between casting lead and silver, Michael Briggs did a blog series on the topic 15 years ago (give or take). He went over the engineering problems with casting silver, made up some test bullets, and did some test fires. It's a non trivial problem.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to say that if an organization with significant resources was taking a crack at sniping with silver, they wouldn't just carefully design the bullet, they'd custom design a rifle for the challenges of firing silver bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T01:03:56-08:00","id":1530875,"title":"","content":"There are numerous ways to make silver bullets lethal and viable. One could essentially make 50 caliber varmint grenades. Varmint grenades have a metal jacket with powdered metal inside and are used to disintegrate small animals. Fill it with powdered silver and it\u2019s going to be extremely lethal to Garou and avoiding the issue of engineering silver bullets. <br /> <br /> Silver sabots could also avoid that problem but may not be as devastating. <br /> <br /> Really though, alpha strikes are not something that should be used against player characters. It\u2019s just not any fun. It might be fun, though, for players to plan an alpha strike against otherwise unbeatable NPCs as long as it isn\u2019t used to cheapen the thematic value of major villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T11:12:24-08:00","id":1530914,"title":"","content":"It's more of an academic discussion than a game-play discussion that spun off of some of the design changes made in WoD5e (esp. W5) that are attributed to disruptive players in LARPs using powers to alpha strike characters (the apocryphal &quot;Garou Umbra ambushes the Prince before the vampires could do anything&quot; story), and how mundane means didn't really get changed the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T13:40:06-08:00","id":1531001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1530787#post1530787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Check the entry for The Slug in the talens of Hammer and Klaive. It's a footnote to it, oddly enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I looked it up, but at least the description says nothing about it doing agg damage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T10:43:10-08:00","id":1531026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531001#post1531001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I looked it up, but at least the description says nothing about it doing agg damage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The text refers its function back to the fang dagger. Fang daggers, when activated, double the damage and make it agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T11:52:37-08:00","id":1531031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531026#post1531026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The text refers its function back to the fang dagger. Fang daggers, when activated, double the damage and make it agg.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says it doubles the damage like fan dagger and that that it is only activated for one shot like a fang dagger.<br /> You can interpret that as doing agg damage but I it is not explicitly said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T11:55:17-08:00","id":1531032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531031#post1531031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says it doubles the damage like fan dagger and that that it is only activated for one shot like a fang dagger.<br /> You can interpret that as doing agg damage but I it is not explicitly said.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's WoD books for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T14:47:57-08:00","id":1531034,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you're making The Slug talens for a high powered sniper rifle... Lethal vs. Aggravated damage isn't going to matter all that much. Most things in the WoD are either going be unable to soak either, or soak both, but even for those that can soak Lethal but not Agg, the sheer volume doubling damage does means it probably doesn't matter. Very few things in the WoD are going to be OK if you fill them up with Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T01:30:26-08:00","id":1531049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531034#post1531034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if you're making The Slug talens for a high powered sniper rifle... Lethal vs. Aggravated damage isn't going to matter all that much. Most things in the WoD are either going be unable to soak either, or soak both, but even for those that can soak Lethal but not Agg, the sheer volume doubling damage does means it probably doesn't matter. Very few things in the WoD are going to be OK if you fill them up with Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The doubling is only for the Pistol version which is level 4 fetish, the Slug talens incrase the damage only by 4.<br /> <br /> And I'm not even sure that the doubling is that strong on a pistol, since the damage of Pistols is iirc not that great to begin with.<br /> It being agg damage or not would at least make a big differnce against vampires.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T22:20:12-08:00","id":1531091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531049#post1531049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The doubling is only for the Pistol version which is level 4 fetish, the Slug talens incrase the damage only by 4.<br /> <br /> And I'm not even sure that the doubling is that strong on a pistol, since the damage of Pistols is iirc not that great to begin with.<br /> It being agg damage or not would at least make a big differnce against vampires.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pistols are 4 to 6, maybe one more for hand cannons. You could probably make a rifle or shotgun as a level 5 version; load slugs in the latter, and you're off to the races for blowing vampires up without needing to run to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T19:21:29-08:00","id":1531166,"title":"","content":"Why use a 50 caliber? With supernatural-senses and abilities, you can easily acquire a nuke; take that 4th generation vamp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T01:21:21-08:00","id":1531179,"title":"","content":"Presumably because you want to take out one target, not a whole city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T20:52:34-08:00","id":1531220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531166#post1531166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why use a 50 caliber? With supernatural-senses and abilities, you can easily acquire a nuke; take that 4th generation vamp.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rFeVfwDvTyM\" data-code=\"rFeVfwDvTyM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rFeVfwDvTyM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> A nuke isn't an assassination tool, it's a WMD. It's also thoroughly unnecessary to take out a 4th gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T19:51:17-08:00","id":1531267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1531179#post1531179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably because you want to take out one target, not a whole city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're not going to take out a whole city with a nuke; most nukes are tac-nukes that have only kilo-ton yields. You'll only take out a few blocks, and especially one that you can smuggle; the MT ones are too big to transport with a bomber or an ICBM. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T21:51:08-08:00","id":1531272,"title":"","content":"Besides how flippant you seem to be about weapons that would be killing hundreds or thousands of people in the immediate blast range, you're also completely dismissing the impact of immediate and long term ionizing radiation on both the area and everything living there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T11:01:24-08:00","id":1531297,"title":"","content":"Really, there are a lot of complications attaining a nuclear weapon as well as detonating one.<br /> <br /> Assuming that you manage to do it, you would be hunted by every supernatural and every mundane organization in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T14:01:39-07:00","id":1539339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1527039#post1527039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampires have the advantage of being magically less impacted by guns (though the ST might rule otherwise for these sorts of firearms), and there aren't that many ways to make bullets do agg (though with something like WtA Talens that's a bit ST dependent, but the examples in the books don't really support just a flat out upgrade like that; mages and changelings are more troublesome as snipers... but they need sniping for these things even less anyway). Vampires are also naturally night time city dwellers. SWAT snipers don't bother training in shooting beyond 300m because cities and suburbs never provide that kind of clear line of sight. Most militarized police around the world aren't allowed to shoot farther than 100m without explicit permission because populated areas have too many complications for the risk. Most powerful vampires don't have to worry about being sniped from a mile away because cities are natural cover, and the closer the sniper has to be, the more those big honking .50 cals aren't practical even with some supernatural boosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the shooter/spotter side, this reminds me of KismetRose's version of kindred lore in which all vital fluids, including tears and vitreous ichor, would be composed of vitae and wouldn't be subject to things like, drying out or being disrupted by wind or dust. Also, they emphasize the undead state by highlighting how micromuscular movements in the fingertips or focal muscles, microsaccades and the like, as well as more gross interruptions such as breathing, heartbeat, digestive movements and the like wouldn't exist. A kindred's eyes and arms would not get fatigued from trying to make fine adjustments for minutes at a time, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Also also, you don't perspire, so no perspiration/respiration means that your optics will never be thrown off by you keeping your face next to them for minutes or hours at a time. No heartbeat to distract you from hearing your equipment as you adjust it.<br /> <br /> Which I understand, that for a typical lick in a typical gunfight means jack all; but it feels like to a trained marksman, being able to turn off your own heartbeat, breathing, sweat and fatigue and never needing to blink, could translate to some kind of mechanical boost to the &quot;Aim&quot; action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T16:20:27-07:00","id":1539345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527031-50-caliber-sniper-rifles-and-other-mundane-alpha-strikes?p=1539339#post1539339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the shooter/spotter side, this reminds me of KismetRose's version of kindred lore in which all vital fluids, including tears and vitreous ichor, would be composed of vitae and wouldn't be subject to things like, drying out or being disrupted by wind or dust. Also, they emphasize the undead state by highlighting how micromuscular movements in the fingertips or focal muscles, microsaccades and the like, as well as more gross interruptions such as breathing, heartbeat, digestive movements and the like wouldn't exist. A kindred's eyes and arms would not get fatigued from trying to make fine adjustments for minutes at a time, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Also also, you don't perspire, so no perspiration/respiration means that your optics will never be thrown off by you keeping your face next to them for minutes or hours at a time. No heartbeat to distract you from hearing your equipment as you adjust it.<br /> <br /> Which I understand, that for a typical lick in a typical gunfight means jack all; but it feels like to a trained marksman, being able to turn off your own heartbeat, breathing, sweat and fatigue and never needing to blink, could translate to some kind of mechanical boost to the &quot;Aim&quot; action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterbalance - here comes the flash bang/laser pointer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T19:12:04-07:00","id":1539354,"title":"","content":"Aiming in the system is minimal enough that while in theory vampires (and Life mages, and so on) should be able to get a bit of an advantage, there's not a lot of mechanical room to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}